Traverse clipped text runs in document order or in reverse

Textloom compatibility patch for accesskit_consumer-0.39.2.
Base: crates.io accesskit_consumer-0.39.2 (SHA-256 f3da8f27636015191b2264ee1df681503170a632cafd832fdc1edfdd4e3a2fd3)
Upstream project: https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit
Textloom changes are MIT licensed. Apply this patch at the crate root.

The Windows text range provider needs run endpoints to move by semantic
formatting and return clipped search results without walking characters or
converting offsets from the start of the document. Keep degenerate ranges
at their original text run so a caret at a wrap or empty heading retains
its affinity. An italic-only change also starts a new format unit.

